ecials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog\" style=\"color:rgba(26,26,26,1);text-decoration:none\">Blog</a>"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":15,"fontWeight":"500","height":24,"left":414,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":26,"width":110}},"mobile":{"config":{"hide":true},"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":14,"height":22,"left":270,"lineHeight":"1.4","textAlign":"center","top":22,"width":130}}}},{"id":"l_2107","type":"line","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"borderColor":"rgba(230,232,236,1)","left":0,"top":63,"width":960}},"mobile":{"styles":{"borderColor":"rgba(230,232,236,1)","left":0,"top":60,"width":420}}}}]},{"id":"sec_2108","type":"section","responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":8329}},"mobile":{"styles":{"background":"rgba(255,255,255,1)","height":11779}}},"children":[{"id":"t_2109","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"<a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog\" style=\"color:rgba(0,122,102,1);text-decoration:underline\">Blog</a> · Trends, tools and stories"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"400","height":25,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":64,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"400","height":24,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":48,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2110","type":"text-block","specials":{"tag":"h1","text":"GEO vs SEO: What Changes When Customers Ask AI Instead of Google"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":42,"fontWeight":"800","height":154,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.18","textAlign":"left","top":105,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(26,26,26,1)","fontSize":30,"fontWeight":"800","height":147,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.18","textAlign":"left","top":84,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2111","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"What carries over from SEO, what actually changes when customers ask AI assistants, which GEO advice to ignore and how to measure AI visibility with free reports."},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(85,85,85,1)","fontSize":21,"fontWeight":"400","height":98,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":277,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(85,85,85,1)","fontSize":18,"fontWeight":"400","height":112,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":245,"width":380}}}},{"id":"t_2112","type":"text-block","specials":{"text":"By <a href=\"https://www.dijaedadula.com/home\" style=\"color:rgba(0,122,102,1);text-decoration:underline\">Dijae Dadula</a> · November 22, 2026 · 9 min read"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":14,"fontWeight":"400","height":25,"left":160,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":393,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"color":"rgba(120,120,120,1)","fontSize":13,"fontWeight":"400","height":24,"left":20,"lineHeight":"1.5","textAlign":"left","top":371,"width":380}}}},{"id":"eb_2120","type":"editor-blog","specials":{"html":"<div class='dd-article dd-b'>\n<figure class='dd-fig'><div class='dd-shot' style='aspect-ratio:16/9'><img src='https://statics.pancake.vn/web-media-264/b1/c0/ad/ce/204e85d836cd2dea0b1d25fc9530b19a295fe49be7024bfe3d902032-w:1536-h:864-l:58553-t:image/jpeg.jpg' alt='Dark isometric illustration of two platforms joined by a dashed green path: a stack of search result blocks on the left and a block topped by a green-outlined AI answer bubble on the right' width='1536' height='864' loading='lazy'></div></figure>\n<p>GEO and SEO are not rivals. Generative engine optimization (GEO) is the work of getting your business cited inside AI answers, and most of it rests on the same foundation as search engine optimization (SEO): pages that can be crawled, indexed and trusted. What changes is what counts as a win, how you write the pages that matter most, and how you measure the result.</p>\n<div class='dd-brief'>\n<p class='dd-brief-title'>The 60-second brief</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Google says optimizing for its AI features “is optimizing for the search experience, and thus still SEO.” Crawlable, indexed, helpful pages remain the entry ticket.</li>\n<li>The win moves from a click on a ranked link to a citation or mention inside an answer, so pages must be easy to quote and facts easy to verify.</li>\n<li>Google and Bing now report AI visibility for free. Measure it monthly instead of guessing.</li>\n</ol>\n<p class='dd-decision'>Decision: keep your SEO basics, rewrite your ten most important pages answer-first with sourced facts, and add AI visibility to your monthly report.</p>\n</div>\n<div class='dd-tiles'>\n<div class='dd-tile'><b>0</b><span>extra requirements to appear in Google's AI Overviews or AI Mode</span></div>\n<div class='dd-tile'><b>Up to 40%</b><span>visibility gain from the best methods in the 2024 GEO study</span></div>\n<div class='dd-tile'><b>2</b><span>free AI visibility reports: Google Search Console and Bing Webmaster Tools</span></div>\n</div>\n<nav class='dd-toc' aria-label='Table of contents'>\n<p class='dd-toc-title'>In this brief</p>\n<ol>\n<li><a href='#same'>What stays the same?</a></li>\n<li><a href='#changes'>What changes when customers ask AI?</a></li>\n<li><a href='#ignore'>What can you ignore?</a></li>\n<li><a href='#measure'>How do you measure AI visibility?</a></li>\n<li><a href='#check'>Decision checklist</a></li>\n</ol>\n</nav>\n<p class='dd-kicker'>Move 01 · Keep</p>\n<h2 id='same'>What stays the same between SEO and GEO?</h2>\n<div class='dd-move'>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>What</span><p>Crawling, indexing, helpful content and technical basics.</p></div>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>Why it matters</span><p>AI answers draw on pages the system can find and trust. If you are not in the pool, you cannot be cited.</p></div>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>Do this</span><p>Fix crawl and index problems before writing a single “AI-ready” page.</p></div>\n</div>\n<p>Google is direct about this. Its AI optimization guide, updated July 10, 2026, says that optimizing for generative AI search “is optimizing for the search experience, and thus still SEO.” Its AI features page says there are “no additional requirements to appear in AI Overviews or AI Mode, nor other special optimizations necessary.” A page has to be indexed and eligible to show with a snippet; that is the whole entry requirement.</p>\n<p>So the SEO checklist you already know still carries the weight: pages that load and render, no accidental blocks in robots.txt, clean internal links, one clear topic per page, accurate titles and descriptions, and content that a person would find satisfying. Structured data is not required for AI features, but Google still recommends it as part of normal SEO because it supports rich results.</p>\n<p>For other assistants the same logic applies with their own crawlers. ChatGPT search and Perplexity read the web through their own bots, so a robots.txt rule that blocks them keeps you out of their answers. The full crawler table is in <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/how-ai-assistants-recommend-businesses'>How AI Assistants Decide Which Businesses to Recommend</a>.</p>\n<p class='dd-kicker'>Move 02 · Shift</p>\n<h2 id='changes'>What changes when customers ask AI instead of Google?</h2>\n<div class='dd-move'>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>What</span><p>The unit of success, the shape of the question and the way pages are read.</p></div>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>Why it matters</span><p>An answer cites a few sources. Being quotable decides whether one of them is you.</p></div>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>Do this</span><p>Rewrite key pages answer-first, with dated facts and named sources.</p></div>\n</div>\n<figure class='dd-fig'>\n<svg class='dk' viewBox='0 0 640 300' role='img' aria-labelledby='gb1t gb1d' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'>\n<title id='gb1t'>What carries over from SEO and what changes for AI answers</title>\n<desc id='gb1d'>Two columns. Left, stays the same: crawlable and indexed pages, helpful original content, technical basics, structured data for rich results. Right, changes: the win is a citation instead of a click, questions arrive as full sentences, one question triggers several searches, consistent facts across the web matter more.</desc>\n<defs><linearGradient id='gb1g' x1='0' y1='0' x2='1' y2='1'><stop offset='0' stop-color='#1f2224'/><stop offset='1' stop-color='#0a0b0c'/></linearGradient></defs>\n<rect x='0' y='0' width='640' height='300' rx='14' fill='url(#gb1g)'/>\n<text x='24' y='34' class='svg-ax'>EXHIBIT · SEO TO GEO: WHAT CARRIES OVER</text>\n<rect x='24' y='54' width='288' height='222' rx='12' fill='#17191b' stroke='#3a3f43' stroke-width='2'/>\n<text x='42' y='84' class='svg-ax'>STAYS THE SAME</text>\n<text x='42' y='120' class='svg-num'>Crawlable, indexed pages</text>\n<text x='42' y='158' class='svg-num'>Helpful, original content</text>\n<text x='42' y='196' class='svg-num'>Technical basics</text>\n<text x='42' y='234' class='svg-num'>Structured data</text>\n<line x1='42' y1='134' x2='294' y2='134' stroke='#2a2e31' stroke-width='1'/>\n<line x1='42' y1='172' x2='294' y2='172' stroke='#2a2e31' stroke-width='1'/>\n<line x1='42' y1='210' x2='294' y2='210' stroke='#2a2e31' stroke-width='1'/>\n<rect x='328' y='54' width='288' height='222' rx='12' fill='#10302a' stroke='#3fbfa6' stroke-width='2'/>\n<text x='346' y='84' class='svg-ax'>CHANGES</text>\n<text x='346' y='120' class='svg-num'>Win = cited, not clicked</text>\n<text x='346' y='158' class='svg-num'>Full questions, not keywords</text>\n<text x='346' y='196' class='svg-num'>One question, many searches</text>\n<text x='346' y='234' class='svg-num'>Same facts everywhere</text>\n<line x1='346' y1='134' x2='598' y2='134' stroke='#2a5e53' stroke-width='1'/>\n<line x1='346' y1='172' x2='598' y2='172' stroke='#2a5e53' stroke-width='1'/>\n<line x1='346' y1='210' x2='598' y2='210' stroke='#2a5e53' stroke-width='1'/>\n<text x='24' y='292' class='svg-s'>Sources: Google Search Central (2025-2026), GEO study (KDD 2024)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Exhibit 1.</b> The foundation carries over unchanged; what shifts is how success is counted and how pages get read.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>Four shifts matter for a business owner:</p>\n<div class='dd-table-wrap'><table>\n<thead><tr><th>Shift</th><th>Classic search</th><th>AI answers</th><th>What to change</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>What counts as a win</td><td>A high position and a click</td><td>Being cited or named inside the answer</td><td>Track citations and mentions, not only rankings</td></tr>\n<tr><td>The question</td><td>A few keywords</td><td>A full question with context</td><td>Write H2s as the questions customers actually ask</td></tr>\n<tr><td>How pages are found</td><td>One query, one results page</td><td>Several related searches per question (Google calls it query fan-out)</td><td>Cover the subtopics around your main service, one clear page each</td></tr>\n<tr><td>What earns trust</td><td>Links and relevance</td><td>Clear, verifiable facts and consistent mentions across the web</td><td>Add sources and dates; keep listings and profiles consistent</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p>The research backs the writing change. The 2024 GEO study from Princeton and partners, accepted at KDD 2024, tested ways of rewriting web pages and found the best methods raised a source's visibility in AI answers by up to 40%. Adding quotations, statistics and cited sources helped; keyword stuffing did worse than doing nothing. The detail of those methods is in <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/what-is-generative-engine-optimization'>What Is Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)?</a></p>\n<p>In practice, answer-first means the first two or three sentences of a page answer its title question and still make sense if an assistant quotes them alone. Facts carry a number, a date and a link. Each page owns one topic, so an assistant running several related searches finds a clean page for each subtopic instead of one page that half-answers everything.</p>\n<p class='dd-kicker'>Move 03 · Filter</p>\n<h2 id='ignore'>What can you ignore in GEO advice?</h2>\n<div class='dd-move'>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>What</span><p>Special files, AI markup and content chopped up “for the bots”.</p></div>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>Why it matters</span><p>Effort spent on tricks is effort taken from the pages customers read.</p></div>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>Do this</span><p>Check any GEO tactic against the platform's own documentation before you pay for it.</p></div>\n</div>\n<p>A lot of GEO advice sells work that the platforms say they do not need. Google's guide lists several things you can skip for its Search features:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>New machine-readable files:</b> “You don't need to create new machine readable files, AI text files, markup, or Markdown to appear in Google Search.” Google Search does not use llms.txt; it will not help or hurt your visibility there, though other services may read it.</li>\n<li><b>Chunking:</b> “There's no requirement to break your content into tiny pieces for AI to better understand it.” There is no ideal page length; write for people.</li>\n<li><b>Volume plays:</b> producing many pages mainly to influence AI answers falls under Google's scaled content abuse policy.</li>\n<li><b>Ranking promises:</b> Google warns that no third-party tool has access to its internal ranking or AI systems.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For reference, check Google's AI optimization guide <a href='https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/ai-optimization-guide' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>here</a> and its AI features page <a href='https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/ai-features' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>here</a>.</p>\n<p class='dd-kicker'>Move 04 · Measure</p>\n<h2 id='measure'>How do you measure visibility in AI search?</h2>\n<div class='dd-move'>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>What</span><p>Two free reports plus a fixed set of customer questions you test by hand.</p></div>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>Why it matters</span><p>Rankings alone no longer show whether customers meet you inside answers.</p></div>\n<div><span class='dd-lab'>Do this</span><p>Verify both consoles and log ten questions every month.</p></div>\n</div>\n<figure class='dd-fig'>\n<svg class='dk' viewBox='0 0 640 250' role='img' aria-labelledby='gb2t gb2d' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'>\n<title id='gb2t'>AI visibility reporting arrived in 2026</title>\n<desc id='gb2d'>A 2026 timeline from January to December. February 10: Bing Webmaster Tools AI Performance report in public preview. June: Google announces generative AI performance reports in Search Console. June 16: Bing adds citation share, intents, topics and compare. August 31: Google's report rolled out to all websites worldwide.</desc>\n<defs><linearGradient id='gb2g' x1='0' y1='0' x2='1' y2='1'><stop offset='0' stop-color='#1f2224'/><stop offset='1' stop-color='#0a0b0c'/></linearGradient></defs>\n<rect x='0' y='0' width='640' height='250' rx='14' fill='url(#gb2g)'/>\n<text x='24' y='34' class='svg-ax'>EXHIBIT · AI VISIBILITY REPORTS, 2026</text>\n<g stroke='#2a2e31' stroke-width='1'>\n<line x1='60' y1='60' x2='60' y2='190'/><line x1='150' y1='60' x2='150' y2='190'/><line x1='240' y1='60' x2='240' y2='190'/><line x1='330' y1='60' x2='330' y2='190'/><line x1='420' y1='60' x2='420' y2='190'/><line x1='510' y1='60' x2='510' y2='190'/><line x1='600' y1='60' x2='600' y2='190'/>\n</g>\n<line x1='60' y1='150' x2='600' y2='150' stroke='#8a8f94' stroke-width='2'/>\n<text x='52' y='212' class='svg-ax'>JAN</text><text x='140' y='212' class='svg-ax'>MAR</text><text x='230' y='212' class='svg-ax'>MAY</text><text x='321' y='212' class='svg-ax'>JUL</text><text x='410' y='212' class='svg-ax'>SEP</text><text x='500' y='212' class='svg-ax'>NOV</text><text x='566' y='212' class='svg-ax'>DEC 31</text>\n<circle cx='120' cy='150' r='7' fill='#8a8f94'/><line x1='120' y1='143' x2='120' y2='78' stroke='#3a3f43' stroke-width='1'/><text x='72' y='72' class='svg-num'>Bing: AI Performance</text>\n<circle cx='285' cy='150' r='7' fill='#8a8f94'/><line x1='285' y1='157' x2='285' y2='172' stroke='#3a3f43' stroke-width='1'/><text x='214' y='186' class='svg-s'>Google announces report</text>\n<circle cx='309' cy='150' r='7' fill='#8a8f94'/><line x1='309' y1='143' x2='309' y2='112' stroke='#3a3f43' stroke-width='1'/><text x='248' y='106' class='svg-num'>Bing: citation share</text>\n<circle cx='420' cy='150' r='9' fill='#10302a' stroke='#3fbfa6' stroke-width='3'/><line x1='420' y1='141' x2='420' y2='78' stroke='#3fbfa6' stroke-width='1'/><text x='430' y='72' class='svg-ax'>AUG 31: GOOGLE</text><text x='430' y='90' class='svg-s'>rolled out worldwide</text>\n<text x='24' y='238' class='svg-s'>Sources: Bing Webmaster Blog (Feb 10, Jun 16, 2026); Google Search Console Help</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>Exhibit 2.</b> Both major search platforms added free AI visibility reporting during 2026, so AI visibility can now be measured, not guessed.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Google Search Console, Generative AI performance report:</b> impressions from AI Overviews and AI Mode over time, by page, country and device. Google says it rolled out to all websites worldwide as of August 31, 2026. AI feature traffic is also counted inside the normal Performance report under the Web search type.</li>\n<li><b>Bing Webmaster Tools, AI Performance:</b> where your content is cited in AI answers across Microsoft Copilot, Bing and select partners, and the grounding queries behind those citations. Public preview since February 2026; citation share, intents, topics and compare were added in preview on June 16, 2026.</li>\n<li><b>A manual prompt set:</b> ten real customer questions asked each month in ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Mode and Copilot. Log whether you are named, which page is cited and which competitors appear.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For reference, check the Search Console report documentation <a href='https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/16984139' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>here</a> and Bing's announcement <a href='https://blogs.bing.com/search/June-2026/New-AI-Visibility-Insights-in-Bing-Webmaster-Tools-Intents-Topics-Citation-Share-Compare' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>here</a>.</p>\n<p>An honest limitation: neither report shows ChatGPT or Perplexity, the manual prompt test is a small sample that changes from day to day, and AI answers vary by user and wording. Treat the numbers as direction over months, not a score for a single week.</p>\n<div class='dd-bottom'><span class='dd-note-label'>Dijae's rule</span><p>Earn the click first, then earn the quote. A page that is not good enough to rank is rarely good enough to be cited.</p></div>\n<h2 id='check'>Decision checklist</h2>\n<div class='dd-table-wrap'><table class='dd-check'>\n<thead><tr><th></th><th>Before you buy GEO work or start a rewrite</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td></td><td>Key pages are indexed and snippet-eligible in Google, and robots.txt allows the AI search crawlers you want</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>Google Search Console and Bing Webmaster Tools are both verified for the site</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>Your ten most important pages open with a two-to-three sentence answer</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>Every statistic on those pages has a date and a linked source</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>Business name, address and services match across your site, listings and profiles</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>Any GEO tactic you pay for appears in the platform's own documentation</td></tr>\n<tr><td></td><td>A monthly log of ten customer questions exists, with a baseline month</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><b>Success metric:</b> after three months, more of your ten tracked questions name or cite your business than in the baseline month, and AI impressions in Search Console trend up for the pages you rewrote.</p>\n<h2 id='faq'>Frequently asked questions</h2>\n<h3>Is GEO replacing SEO?</h3>\n<p>No. Google says optimizing for its AI features is still SEO, and AI answers draw on pages that can be crawled and indexed. GEO adds a sharper focus on being quotable and measuring citations; it does not replace the basics.</p>\n<h3>Do I need an llms.txt file?</h3>\n<p>Not for Google. Google says its Search does not use llms.txt and that no new AI text files or markup are needed to appear in Google Search. Some other services may read it, so it does no harm, but it is not a priority.</p>\n<h3>How do I know if AI search is sending me traffic?</h3>\n<p>Use the Generative AI performance report in Google Search Console for AI Overviews and AI Mode, and the AI Performance report in Bing Webmaster Tools for Copilot citations. For ChatGPT and Perplexity, test a fixed set of customer questions by hand each month.</p>\n<h3>Does structured data help with AI search?</h3>\n<p>It is not required for Google's AI features, but Google still recommends it as part of normal SEO because it supports rich results. Use it for accuracy, not as a shortcut into AI answers.</p>\n<div class='dd-cta'>\n<p class='dd-cta-title'>Get found where your customers now ask</p>\n<p>Want your key pages rewritten answer-first and an AI visibility baseline set up? <a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/book'>Book a free AI Automation Blueprint call</a> and we will review your top pages together.</p>\n<p>Prefer to learn it step by step? <a href='https://grow.dijaedadula.com/newsletter'>Join the free weekly newsletter</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ol class='dd-refs'>\n<li><a href='https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/ai-optimization-guide' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Google Search Central: Optimizing your website for generative AI features on Google Search</a>, updated July 10, 2026.</li>\n<li><a href='https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/ai-features' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Google Search Central: AI features and your website</a>, updated December 10, 2025.</li>\n<li><a href='https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/16984139' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Google Search Console Help: Generative AI performance report (Search)</a>. Accessed November 22, 2026.</li>\n<li><a href='https://blogs.bing.com/search/June-2026/New-AI-Visibility-Insights-in-Bing-Webmaster-Tools-Intents-Topics-Citation-Share-Compare' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Microsoft Bing: New AI Visibility Insights in Bing Webmaster Tools</a>, June 16, 2026.</li>\n<li><a href='https://blogs.bing.com/webmaster/February-2026/Introducing-AI-Performance-in-Bing-Webmaster-Tools-Public-Preview' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Bing Webmaster Blog: Introducing AI Performance in Bing Webmaster Tools public preview</a>, February 2026.</li>\n<li><a href='https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.09735' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Aggarwal et al.: GEO: Generative Engine Optimization</a>, KDD 2024.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Keep reading</h2>\n<ul class='dd-more'>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/what-is-generative-engine-optimization'>What Is Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)? How to Get Your Business Recommended by ChatGPT and AI Search</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/how-ai-assistants-recommend-businesses'>How AI Assistants Decide Which Businesses to Recommend</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog-traffic-to-chat-leads'>How to Turn Blog and Search Traffic Into Automated Chat Leads</a></li>\n<li><a href='https://www.dijaedadula.com/blog'>See all posts on the blog</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n"},"responsive":{"desktop":{"styles":{"height":7822,"left":160,"top":450,"width":640}},"mobile":{"styles":{"height":11307,"left":20,"top":423,"width":380}}}},{"id":"h_css2121","type":"html-box","specials":{"html":"&lt;style&gt;.dd-article ul{list-style:disc outside !important}.dd-article ol{list-style:decimal out